Implement a new in-memory TypeScript module with this exact API:

```typescript
export type ReservationStatus = "held" | "confirmed" | "cancelled";

export interface Reservation {
  id: string;
  owner: string;
  seats: number;
  status: ReservationStatus;
}

export class ReservationStore {
  constructor(initial?: readonly Reservation[]);
  add(reservation: Reservation): void;
  listByOwner(owner: string): Reservation[];
  changeStatus(id: string, status: ReservationStatus): Reservation;
  remove(id: string): Reservation;
}
```

IDs and owners must be non-empty strings, seats must be a positive integer, and status must be one of the three declared values. Malformed reservations or method arguments must throw `TypeError`. Duplicate IDs must throw `Error`. Unknown IDs passed to `changeStatus` or `remove` must throw `Error`. Preserve insertion order in `listByOwner`; an empty store returns an empty array. The store must copy all incoming records and return fresh record copies so callers can never mutate stored state through aliases. Failed operations must leave the store unchanged.

